  "body": "A few things it might be good to think about having landed #10272:\r\n\r\n* [x] we disabled a few tests. We should fix and re-enable them.\r\n   * [x] sytest: `Outbound federation will ignore a missing event with bad JSON for room version 6`\r\n     #10345\r\n   * [x] sytest: `Backfilled events whose prev_events are in a different room do not allow cross-room back-pagination` \r\n     #10292\r\n   * [x] sytest: `Federation rejects inbound events where the prev_events cannot be found`\r\n     #10357\r\n   * [x] complement: `Outbound federation will ignore a missing event with bad JSON for room version 6`\r\n     https://github.com/matrix-org/complement/pull/152\r\n* [x] There's nothing stopping the queues building up almost indefinitely. We need to figure out what to do if a server can't keep up with the inbound traffic. https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/pull/10390\r\n* We previously had a rudimentary form of this queue which kicked in while we were joining a room over federation (see `room_queues` in `FederationHandler`. I think we should update that code to use the same logic. (parking this for now - we'll revisit it as part of future join work)\r\n* [x] #10295\r\n* [x] The new queues need some monitoring.\r\n* [x] ~~We now only process one event per room at a time.~~ Not expected to be significant\r\n",
